<h1>moderately exponential</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
The measure of computation, m(n) (usually execution time or memory space), is more than any <a href="polynomial.html"><em>polynomial</em></a> n<sup>k</sup>, but less than any <a href="exponential.html"><em>exponential</em></a> c<sup>n</sup> where c &gt; 1.  Formally, m(n) is of moderately exponential growth if &forall; k  &gt; 0 m(n)=<a href="omegaCapital.html"><em>&Omega;(n<sup>k</sup>)</em></a> and &forall; &epsilon;  &gt; 0 m(n)=<a href="littleOnotation.html"><em>o((1+&epsilon;)<sup>n</sup>)</em></a>.
</p>


<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

